## Key captured lines (extracted from the raw log)

### Gates 1 & 2 — green (as expected)

```
[init -> drivers -> fb] using 1024x768 (1024x768)
[init -> drivers -> usb_hid] Connected device: input0 (QEMU QEMU USB Tablet at usb-usbbus-0/input0) POINTER
```

(Gate 2 is printed AFTER gate 3 in this particular boot order — the
QEMU usb-tablet enumeration races the probe's Capture-poll window.
Both are present in the same boot; the run script's matching
`run_genode_until` regex still matches and the gate verdict holds.)

### Gate 3 — GREEN, but NOT for the reason the plan predicted

```
[init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: window detected in demo domain
[init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: panel pixel at (512,14) = 0xff1e1e2e (informational; theme panel_bg == nitpicker bg)
[init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: injecting click at (512,460)
[init -> sponge-de] sponge-de: input event received (button clicked)
[init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: input report confirms press
[init -> sponge_de_probe] sponge-de-probe: PASS
[init] child "sponge_de_probe" exited with exit value 0
Run script execution successful.
```

### Gate-3 failure line the plan predicted — NOT observed

The plan predicted gate 3 would time out at the 120 s `run_genode_until`
budget and the probe would log:

```
sponge-de-probe: FAIL external click did not reach sponge-de
                   (usb-tablet injection missing or input driver
                   path not wired)
```

That FAIL line is **not** present anywhere in the raw log. The probe
never entered observe mode at all — it hit the `inject` branch and
passed.

