## Why this is unexpected (diagnostic observation, read-only)

The plan's W0 ("Verified ground truth (confirmed by reading the files)")
predicted gate 3 RED because of the scenario line
(`run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run` line 317):

```tcl
+ start sponge_de_probe | caps: 100 | ram: 16M
  + config | inject: no | render_iters: 1800
  ...
```

and the matching probe config-driven branch
(`repos/sponge/src/test/sponge_de_probe/main.cc:238-286`):

```cpp
bool const inject = (!_config.valid()) ||
                    _config.xml().attribute_value("inject", true);
...
if (inject) {
    Genode::log("sponge-de-probe: injecting click at (",
                CLICK_PT.x, ",", CLICK_PT.y, ")");
    _event.with_batch([&](Event::Session_client::Batch &batch) {
        batch.submit(Input::Absolute_motion{ CLICK_PT.x, CLICK_PT.y });
        batch.submit(Input::Press   { Input::BTN_LEFT });
        batch.submit(Input::Release { Input::BTN_LEFT });
    });
} else {
    Genode::log("sponge-de-probe: observe mode (inject=no) -- "
                "awaiting external click via the real input "
                "driver path (usb-tablet/ps2 -> event_filter)");
}
```

The empirical log line `sponge-de-probe: injecting click at (512,460)`
unambiguously shows the `if (inject)` branch — NOT the `else` branch
(which would log `sponge-de-probe: observe mode (inject=no) -- awaiting
external click…` and would then either time out or print
`FAIL external click did not reach sponge-de (usb-tablet injection
missing or input driver path not wired)` after ~90 s).

Given the source above, `inject == true` at run time, which means one of:

1. **The `<config | inject: no>` start-attribute shorthand in the
   scenario is not actually delivering `inject="no"` to the probe's
   config ROM.** Most likely cause — the Genode run tool's
   attribute-translation for `<start><config>` may stringify
   `inject: no` in a way that does not become an `inject="no"`
   attribute on the inner `<config>` XML node, or `install_boot_module
   "config" …` consumes the value differently. (Ruled out by reading —
   `genode/tool/run/run:324-327` just joins the args with no separator
   and writes them to `bin/config`; the `<config>` child of `<start>`
   becomes whatever the parser produces. The fact that neither the
   `observe mode` log line nor the `FAIL … usb-tablet injection
   missing` line ever appears is itself the smoking gun for this
   case.)
2. **Genode's `parse(Span, bool&)` does not match `"no"` for the
   `inject` attribute.** Ruled out by reading — inspection of
   `genode/repos/base/include/util/string.h:518-533` shows it matches
   a 6-entry table including `{ "no", 2, false }`, so `"no"` does
   parse as `false`.
3. **The probe binary is stale relative to the probe source.** Ruled
   out — `stat -c %y` shows `bin/sponge_de_probe` 2026-07-25 19:02:11
   vs `repos/sponge/src/test/sponge_de_probe/main.cc` 2026-07-25
   19:01:09, i.e. the binary is newer by ~1 minute, so the source
   change is in the binary.

So the most likely root cause is **(1)**: the scenario's existing
`+ config | inject: no` shorthand does not actually round-trip the
`inject="no"` attribute through to the probe's config ROM. A
single-line run-script fix (e.g. `<inject>no</inject>` element form,
or moving the attribute onto `<start>` itself) would re-establish the
red baseline the plan predicted, without any change to the probe
sources or any host-side QMP infrastructure.

This means W1's design as written ("add host-side QMP
`input-send-event`, drive the click from the host, observe it via
sponge-de's `input` report") would not be the *minimal* change that
flips gate 3 from red to green in the run-script as-is. The plan
owner should decide whether the W1 design (host-driven QMP) is still
the right end state given that:

- the run-script itself has a config delivery bug (separate bug,
  fixable locally in W1's prep work), and
- gate 3 already passes today via the probe's own synthetic Event
  injection, which is precisely the path that W1 set out to replace.

